2.E. The following are examples of actions to support good S s pirit. While the absence of these 
 actions is not necessarily an indication of poor S s pirit, the examples illustrate ways to 
 uphold three core tenets of Spirit of the Game — mutual respect, adherence to the rules, and the 
 basic joy of play : 
 2.E.1. playing safely by actively avoiding unnecessary body contact; 
 2.E.2. working as a team to ensure that all players have an excellent knowledge of the rules; 
 2.E.3. bringing up S s pirit issues with opponents as early as possible; 
 2.E.4. establishing lines of communication to address S s pirit and safety issues (e.g. S s pirit 
 captain pregame and halftime meetings; calling a S s pirit timeout if needed); 
